@* Spam traps for a public enquiry form. Render it inside the <form>. The page model needs [SpamTrap],
   and its handler must skip saving when SpamTrapAttribute.Caught(HttpContext).
   - Honeypot: moved off screen (not display:none, which some bots skip), hidden from screen readers
     and left out of the tab order, so people never fill it in; bots that fill every field do.
   - Timing: an encrypted stamp of when the form was shown, so a form sent within a few seconds,
     or posted without the page, is refused. A fresh stamp is written each time the page renders. *@
@using OptimumEarth.Web.Services
@inject Microsoft.AspNetCore.DataProtection.IDataProtectionProvider DataProtection
<div class="honeypot" aria-hidden="true">
    <label for="hp-@SpamTrapAttribute.FieldName">Leave this field empty</label>
    <input type="text" id="hp-@SpamTrapAttribute.FieldName" name="@SpamTrapAttribute.FieldName" value="" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
</div>
<input type="hidden" name="@SpamTrapAttribute.StampField" value="@SpamTrapAttribute.CreateStamp(DataProtection, DateTimeOffset.UtcNow)" />
@Html.ValidationMessage(SpamTrapAttribute.ModelStateKey, new { @class = "field-error spam-trap__error", role = "alert" })
